Falsifies the `compositor_session` fuzz target's rule that a lie re-copies only the liar.

The defect: `damage_to_screen` drops its first clip, to the client's own surface, and keeps only
the clip to the screen. A client that reports damage past its own edge then makes the compositor
redraw (and, in the binary, flush) other windows' pixels, the bug the function's own comment names.

Expected to fail: "client N's damage ... leaves its window", or an overflow in `Rect::translate`
when the rectangle's origin is near `i32::MAX`.

Replay by hand, from the repository root (`script/falsifications` sweeps Kani harnesses and tests,
not fuzz targets):

    git apply fuzz/falsifications/compositor_session.damage_is_not_clipped_to_the_surface.patch
    mkdir -p /tmp/plant && cargo fuzz run -O compositor_session /tmp/plant -- -max_total_time=600
    git apply -R fuzz/falsifications/compositor_session.damage_is_not_clipped_to_the_surface.patch

Measured 2026-10-04 (UTC) on an M-series Mac, from an empty corpus: see notes/fuzzing-the-services.md.

